'''Muzashi no Kuni no Miyatsuko''' (无邪志国造 or むざしのくにのみやつこ) was a {{ill|Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|国造|12=draft|12=draft}} (provincial governor) that governed the Muzashi Province, which later became the eastern region of {{ill|Musashi Province|ja|武蔵国|12=draft|12=draft}}.

The "Kuni no Miyatsuko Chronicle" in {{ill|Sendai Kuji Hongi|ja|先代旧事本紀|12=draft|12=draft}} mentions both Muzashi no Kuni no Miyatsuko and {{ill|Munagashi no Kuni no Miyatsuko|ja|胸刺国造|12=draft|12=draft}}. Scholars debate whether these represent one and the same or two separate territories. {{Sfn|Ken Shinokawa|2021|p=}} posits that these were independent clans initially but became united under the nation-building efforts during the {{ill|Taihō era|ja|大宝|12=draft|12=draft}} (702 AD).

== Overview ==

=== Names ===
* '''无謝志国造''' - The name used in {{ill|Kojiki|ja|古事記|12=draft|12=draft}}.
* '''武蔵国造''' - Later adapted based on the name "Musashi Province."
* '''無邪志国造''' - Modern spelling using {{ill|Simplified Chinese|ja|简化字|12=draft|12=draft}}.
* '''牟邪志国造''' - Found in "Kuni no Miyatsuko Chronicle" in various manuscript copies.

=== Founding Ancestors ===
* According to the {{ill|Kojiki|ja|古事記|12=draft|12=draft}}, the clan descended from {{ill|Ame no Hohinomi no Mikoto|ja|天之菩卑能命|1=Ame no Hohi|12=draft|12=draft}}, with his son {{ill|Takehiranome|ja|建比良鳥命|1=Takehi-Nateru|1=Takehi-Nateru|zh|建比良鳥命|1=Takehi-Nateru|fr|12=draft|12=draft}} founding Muzashi no Kuni no Miyatsuko.
* The {{ill|Nihon Shoki|ja|日本書紀|12=draft|12=draft}} attributes the lineage to {{ill|Ama-no-Hohohi-no-Mikoto|ja|天穂日命|12=draft|12=draft}}.
* The {{ill|Takahashi Monjo|ja|高橋氏文|12=draft|12=draft}} recounts that {{ill|Ōtamahibi|ja|大多毛比|12=draft|12=draft}}, who served Emperor {{ill|Keikō|ja|景行天皇|12=draft|12=draft}}, was the clan's progenitor.

=== Clan ===
The Muzashi no Kuni no Miyatsuko descended from the {{ill|Musashi clan|ja|武蔵氏|12=draft|12=draft}} and shared connections with the {{ill|Izumo clan|ja|出雲氏|12=draft|12=draft}}. The following branches are linked:
* {{ill|Kasahara clan|ja|笠原氏|12=draft|12=draft}}
* {{ill|Osakabe clan|ja|刑部氏|12=draft|12=draft}}
* {{ill|Hasetsukabe clan|ja|丈部氏|12=draft|12=draft}}

=== Notable Relatives ===
{{Div col|content=
* {{ill|Kasahara no Omi|ja|笠原使主|12=draft|12=draft}}
* {{ill|Mononobe no Emaro|ja|物部兄麻呂|12=draft|12=draft}}
* {{ill|Musashi no Take Shiba|ja|武蔵武芝|12=draft|12=draft}}
}}

